    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Swiss, about 22,000 strong and almost all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pike">pikemen</a>, charged the French guns twice, on the evening of 13 September and the morning of 14 September, and were held by massed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannon">cannon</a> fire and cavalry charges.</li><li>The battle hung in the balance until the Venetian forces under Bartolomeo d'Alviano arrived in the mid-morning, after which the Swiss withdrew in a single large open square.</li><li>The Treaty of Fribourg of 1516, the Perpetual Peace, lasted until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a> and opened three centuries of close ties between the Swiss Confederacy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-of-france">Francis I</a> had a medal struck with the words 'I have vanquished those whom only Caesar vanquished', and asked to be knighted on the battlefield by the Chevalier Bayard.</p></aside>
    </section>

